* opamp_core ICMR-aware unity-gain-buffer step -- `klt sim` circuit BODY (issue #185)
*
* Opt-in diagnostic twin of opamp_tran_sr.klt.spice.tmpl: the same real unity-gain
* connection (Rshort 1 mOhm out->inn), CL and pulse timing, but the input steps
* between two LITERAL levels 0.675600 and 1.260000 that bin/pvt_sweep.py chose
* inside the SAME DUT's measured ICMR window of this very (process, supply,
* temperature) point (`select_icmr_step`: the standard 0.3..0.7*VDD stimulus
* intersected with [ICMR_low + guard, ICMR_high - guard]). One request per point
* because the levels differ per point. The standard slew definition and the
* standard bench are untouched.
*
* The waveform artifact (options.waveforms) carries v(out), v(inp), i(vdd) and
* the saved DUT node voltages; `icmr_sr_extract` applies the validity rules
* (settled endpoints, crossings, slew-limited segment) -- see the README
* "ICMR-aware slew diagnostic". The .meas cards are sanity only.

.option scale=1u

.subckt opamp_dut vdd vss inn inp out ibias
.include "opamp_core.spice"
.ends opamp_dut

Vdd vdd 0 dc 1.8
Vss vss 0 dc 0
Iref vdd ibias dc 5u
Xdut vdd vss inn inp out ibias opamp_dut
Rshort inn out 1m
Vinp inp 0 pulse(0.675600 1.260000 200n 1n 1n 1u 2u)
Cload out 0 2p
